2. Search for Instagram bug bounty reports from the past year by using Google search operators to restrict results to the site hackerone.com and only show pages updated in 2023.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use 'site:' and 'inurl:' along with a date filter.</em>
=>Search queries used:
site:hackerone.com inurl:reports instagram 2023
site:hackerone.com "Instagram" after:2023-01-01 before:2024-01-01
inurl:hackerone.com/reports "instagram" 2023
Why the site: + inurl: + date combination works:
site:hackerone.com restricts results to HackerOne’s domain.
inurl:reports narrows it specifically to individual disclosed vulnerability report pages (HackerOne’s URL pattern is hackerone.com/reports/<id>), rather than blog posts or marketing pages.
Google’s after:/before: date operators (or the UI’s “Tools → Any time → Custom range”) filter by the page’s indexed/crawled date, approximating “updated in 2023.”

3. Find Flipkart coupon pages that are not linked from the main site by using Google dorking techniques to search for 'coupon' in the URL but exclude results containing 'expired'.
=>inurl:coupon site:flipkart.com -expired
Why it works:
site:flipkart.com restricts results to Fipkart’s own domain only.
inurl:coupon targets URLs that literally contain “coupon” in the path (like flipkart.com/myrewards?enableCoupon... or bank-partnership offer pages).
-expired excludes pages whose text contains “expired,” filtering out stale deal listings so you mostly see pages Google still indexes as live/current.

